{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel said.</b> We have had enough — we have perished, we are destroyed, and behold, everyone who approaches the tabernacle of YHWH will die like the burned ones, and who would grant we had died already. Then HaShem said to Aaron, since he is the prince over the tribe of Levi, to warn him lest the Levites cause Israel to stumble. And the sense is to Aaron through Moses, or directly, for Aaron too was a prophet. This section too is a sign that it was in the wilderness of Sinai, when the tabernacle was erected and the Levites were chosen and the firstborn were disqualified."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:13.567031830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}